Certainly, here are the last three lines of the poem "If" by Rudyard Kipling:

"If you can dream and not make dreams your master;
If you can think and not make thoughts your guide;
If you can meet with triumph and not lose doth;
If you can touch the sky with your unbent bow;"

These lines encapsulate the theme of embracing life's challenges and maintaining a positive attitude, even in the face of adversity.
